The following words, terms and phrases, when used in this article, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning:
Nuisance means and includes:
(1) Stagnant water on premises;
(2) Any dead or decaying matter, weeds, vegetation or any fruit, vegetable, animal or rodent upon the premises, which is odorous or capable of causing disease or annoyance to the inhabitants of the city;
(3) The generation of smoke or fumes in sufficient amount to cause odor or annoyance to the inhabitants of the city;
